(BUF-11 (LANGUAGE.md:3607), completing the earlier batch's coverage. The
 earlier leaf ('gen leaf buffer properties') already asserts `X's
 length is X's size` - but only ever right after an append, which is a
 sameness the row's own wording does not license: it names append, set
 byte and clear as the mutations to draw between, so a program where the
 check ALWAYS follows an append is an undeclared rule hiding behind an
 already-`exercised` row. This leaf draws the mutation instead of fixing
 it, and does not care what length/size actually equal afterward - only
 that they still agree, which is exactly the "assert agreement" pattern
 PROCEDURE 6a already recommends, and it holds up whichever of the three
 mutations lands.

 The set-byte branch writes inside the CURRENT size on purpose - an
 index at or past size would exercise BUF-29's write-extends-length
 claim instead, a different row with its own leaf above, and conflating
 the two would make a failure here ambiguous about which claim actually
 broke.)

