(BUF-52: a `buffer` function parameter is the caller's buffer, so `Free`
 inside the function releases the same block the caller sees -
 LANGUAGE.md:3680-3683, the same aliasing FUN-26 already establishes for
 a resize. The function name comes from the value surface's word cycler
 ('gen fresh verb'/'gen written name', gen_collections.vox) rather than a
 fixed phrase - generic despite living in that file, PROCEDURE.md 6a -
 and the parameter and the caller's own variable are two independent
 draws from this file's own buffer-name allocator, so they are never the
 same word.

 A function's body closes on a BLANK LINE, not on its own last period -
 LANGUAGE.md:91, and the collections surface's own 'gen open a function
 definition'/'gen emit' pair already carries the scar tissue (a value
 leaf drawn straight after one that left a clause open, "A function is
 defined at the top level, like a thing" x8 in one campaign, gen_
 collections.vox's note above that helper). This leaf hand-reduced the
 same failure the other way around: written through 'gen join lines'
 like every other leaf here, the function's closing period only closes
 the SIGNATURE clause it opens, leaving `Free {param}.` unclosed at EOF
 rather than at the next statement, and the FIRST campaign this leaf ran
 in turned that into "Unknown variable" a few seeds in - the declaration
 the caller expected was still inside the still-open function body. Fixed
 by borrowing the exact two-blank-line shape ('gen open a function
 definition' before, a bare `'gen emit' of "\n"` after) rather than
 inventing a second one; 'gen join lines' only rejoins for the ordinary
 statements once the function is closed.)

